{"scenario":"pool-after-deploy","description":"inventory pool exhaustion right after an unrelated, healthy inventory release","mode":"graph","recorded_at":"2026-10-18 05:49","duration":92.41,"agent":{"duration_s":51.7,"tool_calls":9,"cost_usd":0.13629059999999998,"input_tokens":91256,"output_tokens":2862,"report":"## INC-043: resolved. Frontend is back to 0% errors.\n\n**Root cause:** inventory ran out of database connections. Every request was failing with `psycopg_pool.PoolTimeout` (10 of 10 connections in use, 37 requests waiting). This is a repeat of INC-019, a known connection leak in stock reservation that exists in every current release. No change caused it, so I resolved the incident without a root-cause change id.\n\n**Evidence path:** frontend (46% errors) \u2192 catalog / checkout (failing, but only because inventory was) \u2192 **inventory** (64% errors, 127 of 198 failures started there, its own dependencies healthy) \u2192 pool exhaustion\n- All 100 recent inventory log lines are the same `PoolTimeout` error.\n- It matches runbook RB-INV-01 and past incident INC-019, which was also fixed by restarting inventory.\n\n**Ruled-out changes:**\n- **inventory v5.1.2** (`chg-c2e6bc6d`, sam, 15 min ago, pgbouncer config bump): not rolled back. The runbook says not to roll back for `PoolTimeout`, because the leak is in every version.\n- **checkout v4.2.1** (`chg-86f89528`, kabir, 31 min ago): not the cause. Checkout's errors all came from inventory.\n\n**Action taken (1 of 3 allowed):** restarted inventory (dry run first, then for real), following RB-INV-01.\n\n**Verification:** frontend was degraded at 8.6% errors after 4s, then healthy at 0% errors on the next two checks (7s and 10s). p95 latency stayed around 112\u2013116ms. That's no worse than the 109ms in the alert, so the restart fixed the errors but not latency, which wasn't the problem.\n\n**Paged:** @sam, platform team (#team-platform). No webhook is set up, so the page was only recorded in the graph and nobody was actually notified. Someone should tell them directly.\n\n**Follow-ups:**\n- Prioritise PLAT-212 (the leak fix). This failure has now happened twice.\n- Check whether the v5.1.2 pgbouncer change makes the pool run out faster.","start_t":27.08,"end_t":79.91},"events":[{"t":0.06,"kind":"start","text":"healthy baseline"},{"t":3.11,"kind":"inject","text":"inventory pool exhaustion right after an unrelated, healthy inventory release"},{"t":27.08,"kind":"alert","text":"ALERT frontend error rate 46%, p95 109ms"},{"t":27.08,"kind":"agent","text":"headless agent started (graph mode)"},{"t":79.91,"kind":"done","text":"agent finished"}],"steps":[{"t":33.99,"n":1,"tool":"rank_suspects","note":"top suspect inventory (score 0.908) via path frontend -> catalog -> inventory","targets":["Service:catalog","Service:checkout","Service:frontend","Service:inventory","Service:payment","Runbook:RB-INV-01","Incident:INC-019","Change:chg-86f89528","Change:chg-c2e6bc6d"]},{"t":36.87,"n":2,"tool":"get_logs","note":"read 100 log entries of inventory","targets":["Service:inventory"]},{"t":37.35,"n":3,"tool":"find_similar_incidents","note":"3 similar past incidents, best INC-019","targets":["Incident:INC-019","Incident:INC-027","Incident:INC-031"]},{"t":42.96,"n":4,"tool":"open_incident","note":"INC-043: Frontend errors: inventory DB connection pool exhausted","targets":["Incident:INC-043"]},{"t":45.68,"n":5,"tool":"restart_service","note":"DRY RUN restart inventory","targets":["Service:inventory"]},{"t":49.08,"n":6,"tool":"restart_service","note":"RESTARTED inventory","targets":["Service:inventory","Action:act-2a4528e7"]},{"t":60.89,"n":7,"tool":"verify_recovery","note":"frontend RECOVERED after 10s","targets":["Service:frontend"]},{"t":65.59,"n":8,"tool":"get_owner","note":"inventory is owned by platform (on call: sam)","targets":["Service:inventory","Team:platform","Person:sam","Runbook:RB-INV-01"]},{"t":65.59,"n":9,"tool":"notify_owner","note":"paged sam (platform)","targets":["T